    "body": "Cause: Control compensation (M13.11) programmed the PART contour under G41/G42 without checking the controller could offset it by the register - an inside fillet tighter than r, a short edge beside an inside corner, or a neck narrower than the tool diameter went straight to the post (alarm or over-cut on the machine).\n\nFix (new `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_comp_room.rs`, called from `contour_comp::push_span` on the programmed ring that the walked centre ring pairs with):\n- corners: every edge has to be long enough for the offset trims at its inside ends, r * tan(turn/2) each (the controller's line-intersection rule). A sharp inside corner between long edges passes. A run of facets tighter than r is refused as an arc with its estimated radius: \"control compensation cannot cut the inside corner at (x, y): its radius 2.000 mm is under the tool's 5.000 mm - use Compensation: In computer\". A short edge beside a sharp corner is refused with the edge length and the length it needs.\n- arcs: every fitted G2/G3 that curves toward the tool needs R >= r.\n- neck: the ring on its own, offset by r toward the tool with Region::offset, has to stay one ring. If it splits, the refusal names the gap at the midpoint of the closest pair of points between the pieces.\nComputer compensation is unchanged. I used the trim rule instead of a flat \"edge shorter than r\" test because it is exact: the flat test refuses legal 90-degree corners and lets steep turns through. The decision is in RECOMMENDED.md.\n\nPinned by camcraft-motion control_comp: sharp_inside_corners_between_long_edges_still_ride_the_control (an L boss and a square pocket still get spans), an_inside_fillet_tighter_than_the_tool_is_refused_by_name (r6 passes, r2 with a 10 mm tool is refused), a_neck_narrower_than_the_tool_is_refused_by_name (gap at (35.000, 15.000)). The motion suite (8/8), the app control_comp suite including the Fanuc golden (4/4) and gate -Tier quick all pass. Staged in the worktree, not committed yet.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
